WEBVTT

00:06:58.939 --> 00:07:02.596
defining each task to be done.

00:07:02.596 --> 00:07:06.509
And they then wrote code, 
usually machine code,

00:07:06.509 --> 00:07:08.776
sometimes binary code,

00:07:08.776 --> 00:07:13.506
which was then sent
by mail to a data center

00:07:13.506 --> 00:07:17.724
to be punched onto
paper tape or card

00:07:17.724 --> 00:07:22.051
and then re-punched, 
in order to verify it.

00:07:22.051 --> 00:07:25.387
All this, before it ever got
near a computer.

00:07:25.387 --> 00:07:30.046
That was programming in the early 1960s.